  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "We have only two completed experiments, both image_only/singleprofile: ResNet50 (acc≈0.208) and ViT-L (acc≈0.227). The core hypothesis of this multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding RNA information improves on image-only predictions. config_031 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) is the cleanest test of this hypothesis because it holds the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) and profile setting (singleprofile) identical to our best baseline (config_045), changing only the addition of an RNA branch (scvi_n200) with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the marginal contribution of RNA. If accuracy improves meaningfully over 0.227, RNA adds signal; if it stays flat or drops, RNA is not helpful under this setup and we should focus budget on image-side improvements (e.g., multiprofile aggregation). Choosing scvi_n200 over scgpt or PCA avoids introducing an additional untested variable, and concat is the most interpretable fusion baseline. This is the highest-information single experiment available given the sparse evidence."
}

